MIRA artifact reference

Artifact selected for Path B

Artifact: Existing MIRA Project 3 MVP
Primary stack: n8n orchestration with model/API tools, Google Sheets/Docs and a Railway-hosted MIRA application
Audit focus: The operational path used to create and deliver one photoshoot-planning result

What the system does

MIRA is an AI-assisted photoshoot-planning MVP. A user completes a brand-identity questionnaire; n8n orchestrates model/API calls that synthesise the answers into a structured shoot plan, moodboard and five-image Brand World. Results are persisted through Google Sheets/Docs and delivered in a Railway-hosted app. This audit focuses on inference, retries, media transfer, storage and idle runtime.

Primary user journey

A user submits the MIRA questionnaire.

n8n validates and routes the input.

Model/API calls interpret the identity signals and produce creative direction.

MIRA generates the structured shoot plan and moodboard/media outputs.

Results are stored and delivered to the user through the app.

Architecture snapshot used for the audit

Questionnaire / form -> n8n orchestration -> model and image APIs -> Google Sheets/Docs/storage -> Railway-hosted MIRA app

This reference describes the previous artifact without copying unrelated Project 3 materials into the lab repository.
